# Computer Home studio (D-152)

Jonathan has a lookdev bench for computer Home (`≥1280`) photoreal plates. **Use these tools when the work is visual stills, camera match, masks, grade, fire/snow loops, or Comfy inpaint.** Do not reach for CSS cards or Spline-as-the-room to fake the cabin.

**Installed / in play:** Blender, fSpy (+ Blender importer), Krita, Affinity Photo, DaVinci Resolve + Fusion, ComfyUI, PureRef, ffmpeg, this Vite kitchen, Chrome 1280/1440.

**Maps:** [`docs/ux/computer-office/STUDIO_PIPELINE.md`](docs/ux/computer-office/STUDIO_PIPELINE.md)  
**Jonathan setup checklist:** [`docs/ux/computer-office/STUDIO_SETUP_CHECKLIST.md`](docs/ux/computer-office/STUDIO_SETUP_CHECKLIST.md)

## Handholding (non-negotiable)

Jonathan has **no DCC experience**. If an AI asks him to click anything in Blender, fSpy, Krita, Affinity, Resolve, Comfy, PureRef, ffmpeg, or Finder/Explorer:

1. Give a **numbered or checkbox** procedure.
2. Assume he does not know menus, shortcuts, or jargon. Name the **exact menu path** (example: Mac Blender → **Blender → Preferences…**; Windows → **Edit → Preferences…**).
3. Say what he should **see** after each step.
4. If the UI might differ, tell him to **stop and screenshot** rather than guess.
5. Never say “just enable Node Wrangler” or “run it through Comfy” without the clicks.
6. One job per message when he is mid-checklist. Do not dump five apps at once unless he asked for the full list.

Agents may run Blender/Comfy/ffmpeg **on the agent machine** themselves when that machine has them. That does not replace handholding when Jonathan must do it on his Mac/Windows.
